messages:
alex_devx: FYI customer reported weird import failures when using our JS SDK from a Deno Deploy function and in Bun apps. They pasted a tiny repro and it blew up on module resolution + crypto.

alex_devx: repro (minimal):
```ts
// deno/mod.ts
import { createClient } from '@redwood-inference/sdk';
const c = createClient({ apiKey: Deno.env.get('REDWOOD_API') });
console.log(await c.ping());
```

alex_devx: Deno error: `Uncaught ReferenceError: process is not defined` coming from our env-detection, and `TypeError: globalThis.crypto.subtle is not a function` when some code expects node crypto APIs. Bun logs: `Error: Could not resolve "node:stream/promises"`.

noah_sdk: thanks, this is a long-standing friction. TL;DR: our published bundle currently mixes node: prefixed imports and Node-only APIs. Deno/Bun accept ESM but dislike node: specifiers (and Deno forbids node: by default).

noah_sdk: proposal:
- publish an explicit ESM edge build (pkg: "edge") that avoids node: prefixes, uses webcrypto APIs, and has no Node-only stdlib usage.
- add an optional thin entrypoint `@redwood-inference/sdk/deno` that is just a tiny wrapper pointing at the edge build and includes an example import_map.json in repo.
- add docs: `docs/devex/deno-bun.md` with copy/paste shims and TS suggestions.

ryan_infra: for Bun: Bun provides fetch + webcrypto but path resolution differs. Bun will try to resolve our conditional exports and sometimes pick the cjs entry. We should ensure package.json exports are explicit, e.g.:
```json
"exports": {
  "./deno": "./dist/edge.mjs",
  ".": {
    "import": "./dist/index.mjs",
    "require": "./dist/index.cjs"
  }
}
```
That allows `import sdk from '@redwood-inference/sdk/deno'` in Deno and Bun.

tanya_build: build notes: create an `edge` build target in tsup/rollup that sets platform to neutral, externalizes node builtins, replaces `node:crypto` usage with a small adapter. Example adapter pattern (in TS):
```ts
// src/runtime/crypto-adapter.ts
export function getRandomBytes(len: number) {
  if (typeof globalThis.crypto?.getRandomValues === 'function') {
    const a = new Uint8Array(len);
    globalThis.crypto.getRandomValues(a);
    return a;
  }
  // node fallback - dynamic import to avoid static node: resolution in ESM build
  // (this code only runs in Node)
  const nodeCrypto = await import('crypto');
  return nodeCrypto.randomBytes(len);
}
```
(note: use top-level async only where allowed; or expose async factory).

noah_sdk: typing issues too: customers using Deno with TS sometimes target `--lib dom` and get DOM fetch types; our lib includes Node fetch overloads that clash. Two quick fixes: ship `types-deno.d.ts` that narrows/harmonizes RequestInit, or use `typesVersions` in package.json to map to a deno-friendly d.ts when TS resolves under certain conditions. Simpler: add a `deno/` example that contains `import_map.json` and `tsconfig.json` guidance (set "lib": ["dom", "esnext"]).

alex_devx: customer asks for immediate workaround they can paste into Deno Deploy. I suggested a tiny shim: create `deno/shim.ts`
```ts
// shim.ts
(globalThis as any).process = { env: { REDWOOD_API: Deno.env.get('REDWOOD_API') } };
// noop crypto adapter if needed
if (!globalThis.crypto?.getRandomValues) {
  (globalThis as any).crypto = { getRandomValues: (u: Uint8Array) => { /* not secure */ } };
}
```
and then import the shim before the SDK. Not ideal but works for short-term.

ryan_infra: CI: I added a small smoke matrix to run in a lightweight job. Example GH Action step: `deno run --unstable -A examples/deno/mod.ts` and `bun --version && bun examples/bun/index.js` as quick sanity checks. We'll gate on these passing for any change touching the SDK exports/build.

noah_sdk: I will open a PR with the following pieces: 1) dist/edge.mjs build + adapter, 2) package.json exports update to include ./deno, 3) examples/demos/deno with import_map.json and tsconfig, 4) docs/devex/deno-bun.md with copy/paste shims and a recommended migration checklist.

ci-bot: created issue RED-3781: "JS SDK: deno/bun compatibility path (edge build + docs + CI)" assigned to @noah_sdk.

alex_devx: one more ask from customer: they run Cloudflare Workers (edge) and want streaming responses from SDK. Workers have limited streaming semantics and no ReadableStream from Node. We should document whether streaming is supported in the deno/bun/worker entrypoints and, if not, provide a fallback.

noah_sdk: good call. I'll include a short section in docs: "Streaming + Edge runtimes" covering supported patterns (use chunked JSON, use callbacks, or disable streaming).

alex_devx: great. timeline: small PR -> docs patch -> CI smoke -> ship canary tag. I'll coordinate and keep the customer updated. Thanks everyone :pray:
